§ 1800.31 Procedures for business information.

(a)In general.[Business information](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=f4c3cbbe94e9752cd794676339b0c219&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:32:Subtitle:B:Chapter:XVIII:Part:1800:Subpart:D:1800.31) obtained by [NACIC](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=651c67e90b16160b6dd5e812c394ed8e&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:32:Subtitle:B:Chapter:XVIII:Part:1800:Subpart:D:1800.31) by a [submitter](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=f4542bd04b16dc2daba472ff43a6d756&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:32:Subtitle:B:Chapter:XVIII:Part:1800:Subpart:D:1800.31) shall not be disclosed pursuant to a [Freedom of Information Act](https://www.law.cornell.edu/topn/freedom_of_information_act) request except in accordance with this section. For purposes of this section, the following definitions apply:

Business information means [commercial](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=265f35fb00c3b0b7db4aa6ed53cbda0d&term_occur=999&term_src=Title:32:Subtitle:B:Chapter:XVIII:Part:1800:Subpart:D:1800.31) or financial information in which a legal entity has a recognized property interest;

Confidential commercial information means such business information provided to the United States Government by a submitter which is reasonably believed to contain information exempt from release under exemption (b)(4) of the [Freedom of Information Act](https://www.law.cornell.edu/topn/freedom_of_information_act), [5 U.S.C. 552](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/5/552), because disclosure could reasonably be expected to cause substantial competitive harm;

Submitter means any person or entity who provides [confidential commercial information](https://www.law.cornell.edu/definitions/index.php?width=840&height=800&iframe=true&def_id=a53121116d948b35590be574a33

